{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Moses called to Mishael.</b> It was stated in Torat Kohanim: from here that the priests do not defile themselves for the dead, for Elazar and Itamar did not defile themselves. And this is difficult, for elsewhere we find that the priests are warned against corpse defilement, as it is written: לנפש לא יטמא בעמיו. And furthermore, Elazar and Itamar were ordinary priests, so why did they not defile themselves for their brothers? And one may answer that what it says, 'from here that the priests do not defile themselves for the dead' — this refers to ordinary priests on the day of their anointing, that they do not defile themselves for relatives, for they have the status of High Priests. And likewise the Rav Bekhor Shor explained regarding ראשיכם אל תפרעו: even though ordinary priests were not warned regarding letting the hair grow loose and rending, for they defile themselves for their relatives on the day of their anointing — behold they are like High Priests. And it appears to me that this is what it says at the end of the verse: כי שמן משחת קדש עליהם."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:56.045892592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}